{
  "name": "input",
  "description": "Send input events to a running emulator.",
  "examples": [
    "Press and release the 'a' key:\n  $ ffx emu input key a\n\nType text:\n  $ ffx emu input text 'Hello, world!'\n\nMove the mouse and click:\n  $ ffx emu input mouse move --dx 10 --dy -5\n  $ ffx emu input mouse click left\n\nSend raw QMP input events:\n  $ ffx emu input raw '[{{\"type\":\"rel\",\"data\":{{\"axis\":\"x\",\"value\":7}}}}]'\n\nTarget a specific emulator and slow down the steps:\n  $ ffx emu input --name fuchsia-emulator --interval 100 key a b c"
  ],
  "flags": [
    {
      "kind": "Switch",
      "optionality": "optional",
      "long": "--help",
      "short": null,
      "description": "display usage information",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": {
        "Option": {
          "arg_name": "name"
        }
      },
      "optionality": "optional",
      "long": "--name",
      "short": null,
      "description": "name of the emulator instance to send input to, as listed by `ffx emu list`. Defaults to the only running instance.",
      "hidden": false
    },
    {
      "kind": {
        "Option": {
          "arg_name": "interval"
        }
      },
      "optionality": "optional",
      "long": "--interval",
      "short": null,
      "description": "time in milliseconds between consecutive key combos, characters and scroll ticks. Defaults to 20.",
      "hidden": false
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Events are injected into the emulator's virtual input devices through the\nQEMU Machine Protocol (QMP), so they go through the guest's input drivers.\nUse `print-input-report` on the target to see the resulting reports.\nOnly the qemu engine is supported.\n\nEach step, such as one key press or one key release, becomes one input report\nin the guest. The exception is `raw` key events given by scancode number:\nQEMU sends each of them as its own report."
  ],
  "commands": [],
  "positionals": [],
  "error_codes": []
}